is this shows the  number of annual publications that have  used zebrafish as a keyword you know  from the different journals and you can  see that you know in 2012 there were  over 1,800 publications that use the BIR  fish as a keyword showing its tremendous  growth in popularity zebrafish made the  cover of science magazine in 2005 again  this shows you know they're increasing  popularity with all of this growth and  all of this use of zebrafish for  biomedical research there's also been  problems as the infrastructure the  knowledge of the organism the culture  techniques the nutrition and the  laboratory practices struggle to keep  pace with just the use of the animal for  other forms of research many medical  researchers and veterinarians that have  worked their entire careers with rodent  models are really unfamiliar with fish  and fish culture and its limitations and  its advantages and so that has created  some problems also  since the model has grown so rapidly  there are a lot of discrepancies between  the different laboratories in how they  treat their fish how the fish are  cultured and the different techniques  that have that go into the research for  example there are big differences among  laboratories in what the animals are fed  how often they're fed and how the you  know growing environments are managed  this has the of the problem of creating  discrepancies between different research  laboratories and also it has the  potential to create problems with the  validity of research you know because  any one of these factors can have  tremendous impacts on research results  and so one of the needs for this  community is to better standardized  research methods for zebrafish husbandry  care and culture and also to better  train individuals within the industry to  use this fish as a model in 2010 at a  u.s. aquaculture meeting in San Diego  California we got a phone call the  zebrafish husbandry association was  having their annual workshop and they  had 